Qore Python module packages
===========================

This is a development snapshot for qore-testing, not a final release.
The runtime package contains the native Qore Python module, QPP compiler
metadata and an ABI-tagged qoreloader extension alias in Python dist-packages.
Both entry points use the same shared object. python3-qore is also provided.
The doc package supplies the API reference and test/example programs.

Build with dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc and the matching Qore 3 SDK. Builds use
the distribution default Python development library; no downloads or host
Python environment are used. dh_python3 constrains the interpreter dependency
to that minor version because the bridge uses CPython's full ABI. An interpreter
minor-version transition requires rebuilding this package. This package does
not certify Python free-threading builds or other interpreter versions.

Full, arch-only, indep-only, nocheck and nodoc builds are supported; cross
builds require a separate host Qore SDK and are rejected. Test builds require
the packaged XML module. Source tests gracefully skip XML when unavailable;
JNI checks load it dynamically and explicitly skip when absent. JNI interop
needs separate qualification with the future JNI package.

Tests cover Qore embedding Python, a separate Python process importing
qoreloader, and installed fresh qcc compilation with named arguments.
Installed tests exclude checkout module paths and use temporary workspaces.
Runtime use requires neither the SDK nor XML/JNI.

Most upstream sources specify LGPL 2.1 or later. MIT supporting files and
adapted CPython internals retain their notices; see debian/copyright and the
COPYING files. Metadata and documentation are corrected to match these notices.

Before general release, qualify other Debian/Ubuntu targets and architectures,
freeze the Qore ABI and test relevant upgrades. No prior module package is
available for upgrade testing. PPA publication requires a published matching
Qore SDK and XML test package, plus source signing and upload.
